<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander III of Scotland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1241">1241</a>–1286</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander III was King of Scots from 1249 to 1286. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-largs">Battle of Largs</a> in 1263 he gained the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Western Isles</a> and the Isle of Man from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-perth">Treaty of Perth</a> of 1266, and his reign of peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and growing trade was later remembered as a golden age. His death in a fall from his horse near Kinghorn left only his infant granddaughter, the Maid of Norway, as heir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-iii-of-scotland.jpg" alt="Alexander III of Scotland" width="320" height="281" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_III_and_Ollamh_R%C3%ADgh.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
